## Era stories (facts to keep)

**design** — Visual design and front-end for clinics, food brands, small businesses (e.g. ENGRENHA+, LM Salgados). Typography, trust on screen, every pixel earning its place.

**hardware** — Bachelor’s / SENAI: 3D printing, CNC, Arduino, vision, mechatronics. Magic Globe / Globo Mágico: Rubik’s Cube robot, web/iPad control, sub-2s solves; open-source angle via `magic-globe`. Metaphor for the whole career: find structure under noise.

**ideyou** — IdeYou (from ~2019): beyond pages into platforms. MioDelivery grew from the **LM Salgados** partnership (first major software client since 2017 — factory + multi-store system under early placeholder brand Hi sistemas, kitchen production panel from a CorelDRAW sketch, pandemic ordering stages, first production PWA) and still runs for a few hand-picked food clients that prioritize quality over quantity. Telecom ERP (billing, boletos, operations). Aurélio / planeja-ideyou (BNCC lesson plans). LinkedIn: Full Stack at IdeYou; tools that had to work every peak hour.

**teaching** — CS teaching while building school relationships (networks, IT services, custom systems). CTI as student/project hub. Explaining forced clearer design.

**platform** — Convergence under isaque.it: sistema (admin SPA), api (NestJS/Prisma), cliente (portal), notify.it, barcode.it. Same care as early design sites, at platform scale.

